name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-yz[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Usage collector health and vendor-drift resilience[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Provider usage collection classifies and survives vendor CLI drift,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]exposes an honest per-collector health state derived from failure [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]streaks, and ACE shows a calm, distinct visual indicator whenever a[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]collector is failing consistently.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]usage_collector_health_and_drift_resilience.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/usage_collector_health_and_drift_resilience.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-yz[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-yz/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collector health domain model in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]health-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health-core: track failure-streak start in the refresh schedule, project[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a per-provider collector_health block into the public snapshot, gate and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-rank CollectionProblem attention on consistent failure, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vendor_drift reason code, and coordinate the sase-core release plus the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-side floor bump.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Drift-classifying probe strategies for all collectors[/bold #D7AFFF]     